    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the \"possible duplicate\" soft-match feature for `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `CheckOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`). Runs after the hard-duplicate check (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`), so any owner reaching it is already known not to be a hard duplicate. It scans existing owners for one sharing the new owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` but with a different telephone; on a match it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to that owner's id (lowest id if several match). No postcode \u2192 no match.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted `checkPossibleDuplicate` between `countNamesakes` and `save` (under `transaction` governance), so the flags are persisted with the owner.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) columns with accessors.\n\n4. **API schema** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` as read-only fields on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct auto-maps them by name (used by both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\n5. **Database schemas** \u2014 added the two columns to `schema.sql` for hsqldb (used by tests), h2, mysql, and postgres.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and the full `mvn test` run reports `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
